</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F5EDDF;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does a game fence cost in Waco?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Most 8 foot game fence in Central Texas runs $4 to $8 per foot installed, which works out to roughly $21,000 to $42,000 per mile. Heavy brush clearing, rocky ground and extra gates push the number up, so we quote it after walking your line.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">Do you charge extra for after-hours emergency calls?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Yes, after-hours and weekend emergency calls carry a $150 to $250 trip fee on top of the repair, depending on how far out you are. If cattle are out on a road we treat it as a priority call and we'll usually have wire back up the same night.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">How tall does a game fence need to be for deer?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Whitetail need a fence at least 8 feet tall to be reliably contained, and Texas high fence rules apply if you're managing deer behind wire. We build game fence at 8 feet with fixed knot wire, which also does a good job slowing feral hogs.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">How long does it take to fence 10 acres?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">A 10 acre perimeter is roughly 2,600 feet of fence. With normal clearing, a crew typically finishes barbed wire in 3 to 5 working days, while game fence or pipe fence takes longer because of the heavier posts and wire.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">Do you clear brush along the fence line?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Yes, we clear cedar, mesquite and brush along the fence line as part of most jobs, and we price it separately so you can see the cost. A clean line makes for a straighter fence and a lot less maintenance down the road.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(42,39,36,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 10px;">What areas do you serve?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">We work out of Waco and cover McLennan, Bosque and Falls counties, including China Spring, Crawford, McGregor, Valley Mills, Lorena and West. Estimates are free and in writing anywhere in that service area.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

